hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17086","Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated it to us, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Aws ibn Aws, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever washes and bathes, and goes early and arrives early, and draws near and listens attentively and does not engage in idle talk, there will be for him with every step as the reward of a year: its fasting and its standing."
"17087","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Aws ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever washes and bathes on Friday, and goes early and arrives early, and walks and does not ride, and draws near to the imam and listens and does not engage in idle talk, there will be for him with every step the reward of a year: its fasting and its standing."
"17088","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, Hassan ibn Atiyyah narrated to me, Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Ibn Aws al-Thaqafi narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: Then he went early and arrived early."
